---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Emphasis from '@/components/motion/scenes/Emphasis.astro';
import { MotionEmphasisReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-emphasis.tsx';
import { MotionEmphasisAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-emphasis.ts';
import MotionEmphasisSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-emphasis.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="emphasis"
  title="Motion: draw attention"
  description="An emphasis replays on each change of state: the press of a button, or the shake of a field when its value is refused."
>
  <MotionStage scene="emphasis" label="Live example: Draw attention" height="sm">
    <Emphasis />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    An emphasis plays its keyframes forward each time an element's state changes. The state is <code>data-state</code>:
    set it to a new value, and the emphasis replays. The presets <code>press</code> (dips to 96 % and returns) and
    <code>shake</code> (shakes sideways by 6 px) are emphases.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<button type="button" data-motion="press" data-state="0">Check</button>
<input data-motion="shake" data-state="0" />

// Each new value replays the emphasis of the element
button.dataset.state = String(Number(button.dataset.state) + 1);

// Or replay it without changing the state
getMotion(button, 'emphasis')?.play();`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    A custom emphasis is a definition with the verb <code>emphasize</code>. The badge of the scene grows to 135 % and
    settles on a spring:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`defineMotion('badge-pop', {
  verb: 'emphasize',
  keyframes: [{ scale: 1 }, { scale: 1.35 }, { scale: 1 }],
  timing: 'spring.fast.spatial',
});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    A replay is a call or a change: React calls <code>play()</code> on <code>useMotion('press')</code>, Angular binds
    <code>[udxMotionState]</code> to the value that changes, and Svelte passes it as the <code>state</code> option:
    <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('press', () =&gt; (&#123; state &#125;))&#125;</code>.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-emphasis">
    <MotionEmphasisReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionEmphasisAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionEmphasisSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="emphasize" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A press uses the fast spatial spring. The shake is a linear curve of 400 ms, so each of its five segments takes 80 ms.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.fast.spatial', 'duration.medium4', 'easing.linear']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, an emphasis is not animated: it applies its end frame.
    The scene still says what happened: the field is marked <code>aria-invalid</code>, and the badge still counts.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An emphasis has no presence: its element stays in the page.</li>
    <li>An emphasis restarts when it is interrupted by default. The <code>interrupt</code> option (<code>restart</code> or <code>carry</code>) belongs to the <code>emphasize</code> and <code>layout</code> verbs.</li>
    <li>Use <code>play()</code> to replay it without changing the state.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
